I got down at the railway station in that small town.
At midday, it was very hot.
I walked from the station looking for the boat jetty.
I was very thirsty.
I saw a small shop by the side of the road.
A vendor was sitting in the shop.
I went near that shop.
"I want a bottle of cold water," I told him.
He took a bottle of cold water and gave it to me.
It cost twenty rupees.
I gave him the money.
Then I asked him for directions.
"Where is the boat jetty?"
He pointed his hand to the right side.
"Go straight, the boat is there," he said.
I thanked him.
I drank some cold water from that bottle.
Then I walked to the jetty.
